    <string name="accessibility_service_label">AutoFlow automations</string>
    <string name="accessibility_service_summary">Performs the taps, swipes and typing in flows you create and start.</string>
    <string name="accessibility_service_description">AutoFlow uses this accessibility service only to perform the taps, swipes, long presses, scrolls, typing and system actions (such as Back or Home) that you put into your own flows, and to show a floating Stop button while a flow runs. It looks at the screen only to find the text field you type into or an element your flow targets. It does not collect, store or share what is on your screen, it never acts on lock, permission or Settings screens, and it acts only when you start a flow or a trigger you set up fires. You can stop any run at any time.</string>
